    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d197">

                <pb facs="0933" n="828" xml:id="pg828"/>

                <head>197. Memorandum From Allen Dulles to
                        Eisenhower<anchor n="1" xml:id="d197-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1959-09-12">September 12,
                        1959</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d197-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d197-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Soviet Guided Missile Estimate</item>
                </list>
                <p>1. The United States Intelligence Board has this week brought up to date its
                    estimate as to the current status of the Soviet Guided Missile Program. I
                    enclose a copy for your information.</p>
                <p>2. In the course of its review the Board made use of a panel of distinguished
                    military and civilian experts involved in our own Guided Missile Program. Their
                    findings and recommendations are also attached.</p>
                <p>3. It occurred to me that you might find this latest thinking of ours of use in
                    preparation for your forthcoming talks with Chairman Khrushchev.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">Allen W.
                            Dulles</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Director</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d197-a1.xml" xpointer="d197-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d197-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d197-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Transmits report on Soviet guided missile estimate. Top Secret. 4 pp.
                    Eisenhower Library, White House Office Files, Records of the Office of the Staff
                    Secretary, CIA.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
